.Dd August 3, 2026
.Dt CMDLINE 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm cmdline_init ,
.Nm cmdline_has ,
.Nm cmdline_last_index ,
.Nm cmdline_get ,
.Nm cmdline_get_full ,
.Nm cmdline_debug_enabled
.Nd kernel command line accessors
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/cmdline.h
.Ft void
.Fn cmdline_init "const char *cmdline"
.Ft int
.Fn cmdline_has "const char *key"
.Ft int
.Fn cmdline_last_index "const char *key"
.Ft int
.Fn cmdline_get "const char *key" "char *buf" "size_t buf_len"
.Ft int
.Fn cmdline_get_full "char *buf" "size_t buf_len"
.Ft int
.Fn cmdline_debug_enabled "const char *channel"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions read the whitespace-separated command line the bootloader
handed the kernel.
The parameters themselves are documented in
.Xr kernel_command_line 7 ;
this page covers only the in-kernel interface for querying them.
.Pp
.Fn cmdline_init
copies the command line into a private 1024-byte buffer and prints it.
A
.Dv NULL
argument is treated as an empty command line.
It is called once from
.Fn kmain
before any other function here; every accessor reports "absent" until it
has run.
.Pp
.Fn cmdline_has
reports whether
.Fa key
is present, either bare
.Pq Li serial_debug
or as the left side of an assignment
.Pq Li root=/dev/hda1 .
Matching is on whole tokens, so
.Li ro
does not match
.Li root= ,
and
.Li serial
does not match
.Li serial_debug .
.Pp
.Fn cmdline_last_index
returns the zero-based token position of the
.Em last
occurrence of
.Fa key ,
or \-1 when it is absent.
Comparing two positions resolves flags that contradict each other on a
last-one-wins basis, which is how
.Li ro
and
.Li rw
are decided:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
uint32_t mntflags =
    (cmdline_last_index("ro") > cmdline_last_index("rw"))
    ? MNT_RDONLY : 0;
.Ed
.Pp
Because an absent key is \-1, that comparison also lands on the right
default when neither flag was given.
This matters at the boot menu: every Substrate GRUB entry passes
.Li ro ,
so appending
.Li rw
while editing an entry has to beat the
.Li ro
already on the line rather than being ignored.
.Pp
.Fn cmdline_get
copies the value of
.Fa key
into
.Fa buf ,
truncating to
.Fa buf_len
\- 1 bytes and always NUL-terminating.
A bare flag carrying no
.Ql =
has no value and fails.
.Pp
.Fn cmdline_get_full
copies the entire command line into
.Fa buf .
.Pp
.Fn cmdline_debug_enabled
reports whether a named debug channel is switched on by the
.Li debug=
parameter.
Channel names are colon-delimited and a parent enables all its
descendants, so
.Li debug=perso:elks
enables both
.Li perso:elks
and
.Li perso:elks:aout .
A bare
.Li debug ,
.Li debug=all
or
.Li debug=*
enables every channel.
Cache the result in a
.Vt static
when the query sits on a hot path; each call rescans the command line.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn cmdline_has
and
.Fn cmdline_debug_enabled
return 1 when the key or channel is present and 0 otherwise.
.Pp
.Fn cmdline_last_index
returns a token position, or \-1 if
.Fa key
is absent, empty or
.Dv NULL .
.Pp
.Fn cmdline_get
and
.Fn cmdline_get_full
return 0 on success and \-1 if the key is absent, carries no value, or the
arguments are invalid.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Gate a driver diagnostic behind a boot flag, caching the lookup:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static int trace_on(void) {
	static int cached = -1;

	if (cached < 0)
		cached = cmdline_debug_enabled("storage:ide");
	return cached;
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kernel_command_line 7 ,
.Xr boot 8 ,
.Xr init 8
